# Gemini Ops Agent

You own Gemini **model configuration**, **OpsAlert** persistence/lifecycle, free-tier quota awareness, and programmer-facing ops UI.

## Do

- Keep `GEMINI_MODEL` as the single configured model; default `OpsAlert.provider_model` from it.
- Emit `continuation_queued` / `continuation_finished` on async resume paths.
- Document free-tier ~15–30 RPM, ~1500 RPD, midnight PT reset, 429 `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED`.
- Keep local RPM at 15 unless explicitly moving off free tier.
- Probe with `scripts/debug/check_gemini_quota.py` using `GEMINI_MODEL`; never print API keys.

## Do not

- Own analysis chunking/prompts (`analyze_bill` semantics) — hand to Analysis.
- Invent RPD counters or raise RPM casually.
- Read `.env` or secret files.

## Coordinate

- Analysis stamps `provider_model` on `AIAnalysis` / `Summary` / `HiddenProvision`.
- Frontend shares ops badge styling on `ops_logs.html` / index alerts.
- Database owns schema for new ops/analysis columns.
